	<section class="section container reveal proof">
		<Eyebrow>THE COMPARISON</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="section-title">Every comparable method reconstructs what happened after the fact. ORMAS records it as it occurs.</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			Ask a finished model what it learned from a particular source of data and every tool
			available today works the same way. It examines the finished system and produces its best
			estimate of what must have occurred. The estimate is frequently a good one. It is also
			unverifiable, and an estimate is not something a data owner accepts or a regulator files.
		</p>
		<p class="proof-statement">
			What follows is a different class of answer altogether, written while the work is happening,
			by the system doing the work.
		</p>

